+  # Cancel superseded runs on pull requests only. main is the release baseline and the
+  # trigger for the Release workflow, which fires on `workflow_run: completed` and refuses
+  # to publish unless CI concluded `success`. Rapid successive merges used to cancel the
+  # older main run mid-flight, which GitHub reports as `failure` with no test having
+  # failed, and made Release skip entirely. Letting each main commit finish is the point.
+  # (A bare `false` here would be a truthy string; the expression is what evaluates to a
+  # boolean.)
